    "title": "Oak Hill Elementary perfects IREAD testing - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Andrew Newland Ryan Canfield ,\n2 hours ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) — After a plateau powered by the pandemic, Vanderburgh County elementary students are returning to school this year with exceptional reading comprehension rates.\nThese are the highest of this decade, as nine EVSC Schools had proficiency rates at 90% or better on the 2026 IREAD standardized tests.\nOak Hill Elementary in Evansville led the way with a 100% pass rate and staff members and officials are exhaling a sigh of relief.\nOak Hill Principal Shannon Strieter says very real tears were shed when the perfection was announced, she attributes the entire Oak Hill community to the triumphant milestone.\n“It was truly a real partnership,” Strieter said. “Their parents were just as excited as we were when we crossed that finish line.”\nAs one of the students who led the way for Oak Hill, Zailee Johnson knows how important IREAD is for her classmates.\n“We should like reading because it is fundamental, it is fun and if you don’t like it then you don’t have to. But, I’m just telling you it’s a great thing to do.”\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
